---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProjectCard from '../components/ProjectCard.astro';
---

<BaseLayout>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="shell hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Technical Product Manager · AI systems · Product builder</p>
        <h1>I build systems that survive contact with <em>reality.</em></h1>
        <p class="lede">
          My work sits between product intent and engineering execution: turning recurring friction into software, making AI-assisted systems governable, and designing for the messy parts that show up after the demo works.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button" href="/work/">Explore the work</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="/about/">How I think</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="hero-panel" aria-label="What I focus on">
        <p class="hero-panel__label">Current operating model</p>
        <dl class="signal-list">
          <div>
            <dt>Build</dt>
            <dd>Useful products around real workflows.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Govern</dt>
            <dd>Bound AI authority with explicit rules and checks.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Verify</dt>
            <dd>Prefer evidence, failure visibility, and repeatable behavior.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Make</dt>
            <dd>Software when software fits. Wood when wood fits.</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Selected work</p>
          <h2>Projects with something to prove.</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="section-intro">
          These are not repository cards dressed up as a portfolio. Each project exists because a real workflow, constraint, or recurring failure was worth solving.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-grid">
        <ProjectCard
          title="Personal Memory Bank"
          href="/work/personal-memory-bank/"
          eyebrow="AI engineering · Developer workflow"
          description="Persistent project context with explicit authority, freshness, provenance, diagnostics, hooks, review workflows, and deterministic guardrails."
          status="Open source"
          tags={['Context engineering', 'Governance', 'CLI', 'CI']}
          tone="forest"
        />
        <ProjectCard
          title="AI Code Review Agent"
          href="/work/ai-code-review-agent/"
          eyebrow="Local AI · Developer tooling"
          description="A privacy-conscious multi-agent review system that isolates specialist perspectives, structures evidence, and makes failure behavior part of the product."
          status="Open source"
          tags={['Local inference', 'Review', 'Security', 'Verification']}
          tone="slate"
        />
        <ProjectCard
          title="Side Quest Atlas"
          href="/work/side-quest-atlas/"
          eyebrow="Product design · Travel memory"
          description="A private group travel-memory product built around low-friction capture, shared history, clear domain boundaries, and durable data ownership."
          status="Private case study"
          tags={['Flutter', 'Supabase', 'RLS', 'Domain modeling']}
          tone="gold"
        />
        <ProjectCard
          title="PitLogic"
          href="/work/pitlogic/"
          eyebrow="Product engineering · BBQ telemetry"
          description="A client-side cook logging and analytics product with live probe integration, alarms, stall intelligence, forecasting, portability, and offline-capable PWA behavior."
          status="Open source"
          tags={['React', 'Telemetry', 'PWA', 'Analytics']}
          tone="copper"
        />
      </div>

      <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;"><a class="text-link" href="/work/">See the full project set, including private case studies →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Working principles</p>
          <h2>Useful beats impressive.</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="section-intro">
          I am interested in the layer between a compelling idea and a system people can actually rely on.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="principle-grid">
        <article class="principle">
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Start with the workflow.</h3>
          <p>Technology should follow the user problem, constraints, and operating environment—not become the reason the product exists.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle">
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Bound authority.</h3>
          <p>Automation earns scope. Consequential actions need explicit limits, deterministic checks, and approval points where judgment matters.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle">
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Make failure legible.</h3>
          <p>Uncertainty, degraded states, and recovery paths belong in the design. Quiet guessing is not resilience.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split-feature">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Research & engineering practice</p>
        <h2>Harness Engineering</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">
          My working framework for reasoning about the systems around AI models: context, memory, instructions, tools, orchestration, governance, evaluation, and execution boundaries.
        </p>
        <p><a class="text-link" href="/harness-engineering/">Explore the framework →</a></p>
      </div>
      <aside class="feature-note">
        <strong>No new machinery without an observed need.</strong>
        <p>Measure first. Use deterministic sources where they already exist. Add telemetry, agents, or infrastructure only when the failure mode justifies them.</p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--warm">
    <div class="shell split-feature">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Outside the terminal</p>
        <h2>Nolan's Workshop</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">
          Jigs, work surfaces, shop systems, furniture, finishing, and the occasional overbuilt solution—because sometimes the right toolchain includes hardwood, steel, sawdust, and patience.
        </p>
        <p><a class="text-link" href="/woodworking/">Step into the workshop →</a></p>
      </div>
      <aside class="feature-note">
        <strong>Same bias, different material.</strong>
        <p>Understand the job, respect the constraints, build for use, and leave enough evidence that the next version gets better.</p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
